# Keepwise project rules

1. Read existing code, these rules, `AGENTS.md`, and `docs/project-context.md` before changing behavior.
2. Keepwise is a personal ownership assistant (assets, purchases, warranties, maintenance, insurance, reminders). Reminder reliability and confirm-first capture are core values.
3. Do not introduce microservices, extra component libraries, or password authentication.
4. Do not over-engineer. Reuse existing patterns. Do not modify unrelated files.
5. Never commit secrets, `.env` files with secrets, or connection strings with production credentials.
6. Never expose secrets in logs.
7. Never remove tests to make a build pass. Never disable warnings just to compile.
8. Keep business logic in `Keepwise.Domain` / `Keepwise.Application` and behind provider abstractions.
9. For significant changes, plan first (save the plan in `docs/plans/` only), then implement, then tests, then docs.
10. Do not force-push without explicit approval. Do not discard uncommitted user work.
11. ASP.NET Core 10 is the only backend. Dates are calculated on the backend (source of truth).
12. Users may only access their own data.
13. Update `docs/` and ADRs if architecture or conventions change.
